1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was the eldest son of Mursili II and Queen Gassulawiya, and he had several siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is best known as the Hittite ruler who fought Ramesses II to a standstill at the Battle of Kadesh around 1274 BC. Aside from the battle with Egypt, he is best known for relocating the Hittite capital to Tarhuntassa[1] and appoi
2 CONC nting his brother Hattusili as governor in Hattusa.
2 CONT
2 CONT A copy of a treaty has been recovered between him and Alaksandu, ruler of Wilusa (Troy), one of the Arzawa lands.
2 CONT
