1 NOTE 	1  NAME the Great //
2 CONT 	2  GIVN the Great
2 CONT 	2  SURN
2 CONT 	2  NICK the Great
1 NOTE He reigned 1279-1212 BC, ancient Egyptian king, third ruler of the 19th 
2 CONT Dynasty. During the early part of his reign Ramses fought to regain the 
2 CONT territory in Africa and western Asia that Egypt had held during the 16th 
2 CONT and 15th centuries bc. His principal opponents were the Hittites, a 
2 CONT powerful people of Asia Minor, against whom he waged a long war. The major 
2 CONT battle of this war was fought in 1274 at Kadesh, in northern Syria, and 
2 CONT was hailed by Ramses as a great triumph. Neither power achieved a 
2 CONT conclusive victory, however, and in 1258 bc a treaty was signed whereby 
2 CONT the contested lands were divided and Ramses agreed to marry the daughter 
2 CONT of the Hittite king. The remaining years of his rule were distinguished by 
2 CONT the construction of such monuments as the rock-hewn temple of Abu Simbel, 
2 CONT the great hypostyle hall in the Temple of Amon at al-Karnak, and the 
2 CONT mortuary temple at Thebes, known as the Ramesseum.
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT http://www.american-pictures.com/genealogy/persons/per00709.htm#0
1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT Pharoah SEP 1279(1295?)-1213 BCE
1 NOTE He was Pharoah from Sep 1279 to Jul 1213 BC. His name was Ousimare Setpenre Ramessou II.
1 NOTE He was Pharoah from Sep 1279 to Jul 1213 BC. His name was Ousimare Setpenre Ramessou II.
