1 NOTE RAMSES II  User maat ra/setep en ra /Amen mer/Ra mes sse s
2 CONT Died at age 96 years, having reigned 67 years. The start of his reign is known to be day 27 of month 6 (Shomu) (rougly June- the sothic calander was in perfect synchronism in 1321, so in the 17 years from 1321 to 1304 BC the calen
2 CONC dar would have shifted 4 days, i.e.instead of 27 June it would have been 23 June with one day further allowance since Shomu starts day 180 of cycle not day 181 as does June so 24 June 1304.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a fixed date New moon festival on day 27 of month 6 (Shomu)-note synchronism with start of reign also - in Year  52 Ramses II. This can occur only in 1252 BC, 1238, 1227, 1220, 1209, etc, and other dates on either side of
2 CONC  that sequence. These imply start dates on 1304, 1290, 1279, etc. While some scholars use 1279, this cannot be reconciled with the earlier dates, and
2 CONT only 1304 is possible. Cambridge Ancient History agrees with this and see their explaination for details. Also See Journal Near East Studies Vol 25
2 CONT p 51 (14 pages) and JNES 45 #2 (1986) p 139. The rise of Sirus in 1539 +/- 4 years Amenhotep I fixes his reign to start 1548, and actually 22 Jul 1548.
2 CONT There also is a fixed Lunar date in Thuthmose III fixing his start date to 19 May 1504. (see Thuthomse III and AmenHotep I for details)
2 CONT
2 CONT There was a Lunar Eclipse recorded in 14 Takelot II which was 24 Feb 822 BC.
2 CONT This fixes the reign to 836 start date. JNES Vol 24 p 61 (1967)
