2 CONT Suppiluliuma I was king of the Hittites (r. c. 1344–1322 BC). He achieved fame as a great warrior and statesman, successfully challenging the then-dominant Egyptian empire for control of the lands between the Mediterranean and the
2 CONC  Euphrates.
