1 NOTE He reigned 1291-1279 BC, ancient Egyptian king, second ruler of the 19th 
2 CONT Dynasty, the son and successor of King Ramses I (ruled 1293-1291 bc). From 
2 CONT 1292 bc he ruled as coregent with his father for a short time. He tried to 
2 CONT recover some Syrian possessions Egypt had lost during the internal 
2 CONT dissensions at the close of the 18th Dynasty. Later in his reign, Seti 
2 CONT conquered Palestine, defended his western frontier against the Libyans, 
2 CONT and fought against the Hittites. Seti's magnificent tomb in the Valley of 
2 CONT the Kings, near Thebes, and his temple at Abydos are impressive 
2 CONT architectural monuments. His mummy was found in 1881 at Dayr al-Bahri.
1 NOTE known reign 15 years, known he died day 27 of the 6th month (Shomu)- roughly June, so we still know his reign exactly.
