1 NOTE He reigned 1182-1151 BC, Egyptian king of the 20th Dynasty, a great 
2 CONT military leader who repeatedly saved the country from invasion. In the 
2 CONT fifth year of his reign, Ramses defeated an attack by the Libyans from the 
2 CONT west, and two years later he routed invaders known as the Sea Peoples. In 
2 CONT his 11th year he again repelled an attempted Libyan invasion. Ramses was 
2 CONT also a builder of temples and palaces in the tradition of his 19th-Dynasty 
2 CONT predecessor, Ramses II. His victories are depicted on the walls of his 
2 CONT mortuary temple at Medinet Habu, near Luxor. Egyptian records tell of a 
2 CONT strike by workers at Ramses's burial site and of a plot against the king 
2 CONT near the end of his reign. Ramses III was the last of the great rulers of 
2 CONT ancient Egypt; his death was followed by centuries of weakness and foreign 
2 CONT domination.
