2 CONT Ramses I (reigned 1307-1306 bc), ancient Egyptian king, first ruler of the 19th Dynasty. Ramses was a general under his predecessor, the childless King Haremhab. He came from a family of the eastern Delta region and was probably a
2 CONC  native of the city of Avaris. Ramses’s reign was too short to leave many monuments, although he built a small chapel at Abydos and carved a few reliefs on the back of the second pylon (pyramid gateway) at Al Karnak. His son, Seti
2 CONC  I, succeeded him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 1306 BC
