2 CONT The unusual mummification of unknown man E, believed to be Pentawere, points to a "nonroyal burial" that includes use of goat skin to cover his body. The procedure appears to be a punishment for conspiring against the king, accord
2 CONC ing to the study. "Use of goat or sheep skins in dynastic burials was rare because these materials were regarded ritually impure," it says. A genetic study shows they had common lineage.
