1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tentamun (20th dynasty) From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia T
2 CONT n t 	i 	mn n 	B1 [1] Tentamun in hieroglyphs
2 CONT
2 CONT Tentamun (“she of Amun”) was an ancient Egyptian queen, most likely the wife of Ramesses XI, last ruler of the 20th dynasty. She is mentioned on the funerary papyrus of her daughter Duathathor-Henuttawy, who was the wife of Pinedj
2 CONC em I and probably the daughter of Ramesses XI. Tentamun's name is written in a cartouche.[2] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT A man named Nebseni is mentioned as her father on the funerary papyrus of her daughter.[3] He was probably buried in the Theban tomb TT320.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her children are:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Duathathor-Henuttawy, who was the wife of Pinedjem I[3]
2 CONT     Another possible daughter is Tentamun, the wife of Smendes.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tentamun_(20th_dynasty)]
