2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=jdp-fam&id=I62292
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Pinudjem II Titkheperre, High Priest of Egypt, was born circa 1015 BC.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT This king and the founder of the 22nd Dynasty dispatched a certain Ma (ie. Libyan) subordinate named Wayheset to the desert oasis town of Dakhla in order to restore the king's authority over the western oasis region of Upper Egypt
2 CONC . Wayheset's titles include Prince and Governor of the Oasis. His activities are recorded in the Large Dakhla stela. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This stela states that Wayheset adjudicated in a certain water dispute by consulting a land-register which is explicitly dated to Year 19 of a "Pharaoh Psusennes" in order to determine the water rights of a man named Nysu-Bastet.
2 CONT --------------------
