2 CONT '''Darius''' (Old Persian: 𐎭𐎠𐎼𐎹𐎺𐎢𐏁 Dārayavaʰuš; Greek: Δαρεῖος Dareios; c. 485 – 465 BCE), was crown prince of the Persian Empire. He was the eldest son of the Persian king Xerxes I and his wife Amestris, the daughter of Onophas. 
2 CONC His younger brothers were Hystaspes and Artaxerxes, and his younger sisters were Rhodogyne and Amytis.
2 CONT
