1 NOTE He was called Codomannus. He was placed on the throne by the eunuch Bagoas 
2 CONT (died 336? bc), following the latter's assassinations of Artaxerxes III 
2 CONT (reigned 358?-338 bc), who had reigned for 20 years, and Arses (died c. 
2 CONT 336 bc), who had reigned for two years; Darius, in turn, killed Bagoas. In 
2 CONT the course of his 6-year reign Darius III led the Persian army against the 
2 CONT forces of Alexander the Great of Macedonia but was defeated at the battles 
2 CONT of Issus in 333 bc and Gaugamela in 331. He was killed by one of his own 
2 CONT satraps while fleeing from Gaugamela.
