2 CONT NameSanatroukes "the Apostle-killer" King of Armenia
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth65
2 CONT
2 CONT Death117
2 CONT
2 CONT FatherMeherdates King of Armenia
2 CONT
2 CONT Misc. Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT renounced Christianity, under pressure from his lords and pagan clergy, and put his daughter to death 
2 CONT
2 CONT SANATRUCES (Sinatruces, Pers. Sanatruk), Parthian king. In the troublous times after the death of Mithradates II. (c. 88 B.c.) he was made king by the Sacaraucae, a Mongolian tribe who had invaded Iran. in. 76 B.C. He was eighty y
2 CONC ears old and reigned seven years; his successor was his son Phraates III. (Lucian, Macrob. 15; Phlegon, fr. 12 ap. Phot. cod. 97; Appian, Mithr. 104; Dio Cass. xxxvi. 45). Another Sanatruces (Sanatrucius) is mentioned as an epheme
2 CONC ral Parthian king in A.D. 115 (Malalas, Chron. p. 270, 273). (Eo. M.) http://69.1911encyclopedia.org/S/SA/SANATRUCES.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses
2 CONT
2 CONT ChildrenGhadama
