2 CONT =Sextus Cocceius Anicius Faustus Paulinus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sextus Cocceius Anicius Faustus Paulinus (fl. 3rd century AD) was a Roman senator who was appointed suffect consul sometime before AD 260/268.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably either the son or nephew of Anicius Faustus Paulinus, suffect consul before AD 230, Faustus Paulinus was a member of the Patrician 3rd century gens Anicia. He was appointed suffect consul sometime before AD 260/268, and w
2 CONC as the proconsular governor of Africa, most likely around AD 265/268, but it has been acknowledged that he may have filled the office sometime later, possibly between AD 276 and 285.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been speculated that he was possibly the father of Anicius Faustus Paulinus, the consul of AD 298.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sextus_Cocceius_Anicius_Faustus_Paulinus
