1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Amnius Nicomachus Paulinus Anicius=
2 CONT
2 CONT Amnius was born in year 0294.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT + B: Abt. 294
2 CONT
2 CONT Amnius' father was Amnius Julianus Anicius and his mother was Caesonia Manilia.  His paternal grandparents were Sextus Faustus Paulinus Anicius and Amnia Demetrias; his maternal grandparents were  L. C. Ovinius R. M. Bassus and  J
2 CONC unia Maximus.  He was an only child.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amnius' family with Auchenia Bassa Bassus
2 CONT
2 CONT They had a son named Anicius.
2 CONT
2 CONT Male Prefect of the Roman Empire Anicius Auchenius Bassus
2 CONT
2 CONT Anicius was born in year 0314.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT + Birth Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT # B: Abt. 314
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 http://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=PED&db=jdp-fam&id=I82362&style=TABLE
2 CONT
2 CONT This page is within a frameset. View the entire genealogy report of Anicius families, or surname index of Anicius pedigrees or report summary of Anicius heritage from "The Skaggs-Files".
2 CONT family history.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Amnius Anicius Paulinus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Amnius Anicius Paulinus, full name Amnius Manius Caesonius Nicomachus Anicius Paulinus Honorius (fl. 334–335) was a politician of the Roman Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Paulinus was the son of Amnius Anicius Julianus, consul in 322, and the nephew of Sextus Anicius Faustus Paulinus, consul in 325. He was thus a member of the gens Anicia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Paulinus was consul in 334 and praefectus urbi of Rome in 334–335. In 334 he erected an equestrian statue to emperor Constantine I in the Roman Forum; a statue was dedicated to him in the Forum of Trajan, whose inscription celebra
2 CONC tes Paulinus for "his high birth, his eloquence, his fairness, and his good judgement, for which he is renowned in private and in public".
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian Settipani has tried to reconstruct Paulinus' familiar bonds. According to Settipani, Paulinus was married to Pincia (born ca 305) or better, to Auchenia. His wife was perhaps the daughter of Pincius (b. ca 280 and c.v. i
2 CONC n the beginning of the 4th century) and wife Caeionia (b. 285 or 290), in turn perhaps the daughter of (Marcus) Caeionius Proculus, suffect consul of Rome in 289, and wife Alfenia Juliana.
2 CONT
2 CONT They were perhaps the parents of Anicius Auchenius Bassus, praefectus urbi of Rome in 382.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amnius_Anicius_Paulinus
