2 CONT
2 CONT In Islam, Abd al-Uzza ibn Qusai (Arabic: عبد العزى بن قصي) forms an important link between his father, Qusai ibn Kilab (c. 400–480), the great-great-grandfather of Shaiba ibn Hashim (Abd al-Mutallib) and his son Asad ibn Abd al-Uz
2 CONC za.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Abd al-Uzza derives from one of the three chief gods of Arabian religion in pre-Islamic times, al-Uzza.[2]
