1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Asad ibn Hashim (Arabic: أسد بن هاشم‎) was the son of Hashim ibn Abd al-Manaf and the brother of Abdul Muttalib. He was the father of Fatima bint Asad, the mother of Ali and the cousin and wife of Abu Talib. Asad i
2 CONC bn Hashim descendants usually use the surname "Qureshi", "Hashmi" or "al-Hashmi al-Asadi", while some of his descendants avoid using any surname. Al-Sheikh Al-Kabir Sheikh-ul-Islam Baha-ud-din Zakariya Al-Qureshi is a famous Sufi 
2 CONC saint who is one of his descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://bit.ly/1iQhZWQ
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asad_ibn_Hashim]
2 CONT
2 CONT Asad ibn Hashim (Arabic: أسد بن هاشم‎) was the son of '''Hashim ibn Abd al-Manaf, the great-grandfather of the Islamic prophet Muhammad and the brother of Abdul Muttalib, grandfather of the Islamic prophet Muhammad'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of Fatima bint Asad, the mother of Ali and the cousin and wife of Abu Talib. Asad was a very respectful person among the Qureshi Arab tribe. He was a merchant and very often helped the poor. His name means Lion (
2 CONC a brave one). His descendants usually use the surname "Qureshi", "Hashmi" or "al-Hashmi al-Asadi", while some of his descendants avoid using any surname.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents 1	Birth 2	Religion 3	Brothers and sisters 4	Descendants 5	Death 6	References Birth Historians are not clear about his exact date of birth, but according to the sources he was born in 485AD or 497AD in Mecca.
2 CONT
2 CONT Religion According to sources he was of the religion of Abraham, as most of the Arabs were of Abraham's religion, including his tribe Quresh and his other uncles. Asad died before the birth of Muhammad.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brothers and sisters Abu Saifi bin Hashim Abd al-Muttalib bin Hashim Nazil bin Hashim Nadla binte Hashim Safia binte Hashim Shifa binte Hashim Ruqayya binte Hashim Khalidah binte Hashim Hannah binte Hashim Zaifah binte Hashim Jann
2 CONC a binte Hashim Ramlah binte Hashim Hayyah binte Hashim Da'ifah binte Hashim Sayfah bin Hashim Abbas bin Hashim Abu Sayr bin Hashim Descendants Fatimah bint Asad bin Hashim She was the mother of Caliph Ali and his brothers. Fatimah
2 CONC  bint Asad was very dear to Muhammad.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hunain bin Asad bin Hashim[1] Hunain was a son of Asad, and he had two sons, Abdullah and Abd-ur Rahman. They both were Sahabi and Abdullah and Abdullah's son name are mentioned in many books of Ahadith.[2] From the sons of Hunain
2 CONC , Abd-ur Rahman was the ancestor of the famous saint of the sub-continent Sheikh-ul-Islam Bahauddin Zakariya.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adai bint Asad bin Hashim (mother of Haninai al-Nehar Peḳkod ben Bustanai bar Adai, Exilarch and Gaon of Sura, Syria) Khalda bint Asad bin Hashim (she married her cousin Al-Arqam bin Nazil bin Hashim and had a daughter named Um al
2 CONC -Saaib Al-Shafaa)[3] Habbar bin Assad bin Hashim (he married his cousin Sa'd bint Abi Sayfi bin Hashim and had a son named Abdul-Rahman bin Habbar)
