2 CONT Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hasim ibn Abd Manaf al-Qurayshi[2] (Arabic: حَمْزَة إبْن عَبْد ٱلْمُطَّلِب, romanized: Ḥamza ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib; c. 568 – 625)[3][1] was a foster brother, paternal uncle, maternal second-cousin, and
2 CONC  companion of the Islamic prophet Muhammad.
