2 CONT
2 CONT Carried on the traditional duties of being head of the diplomatic department (to represent ''Quraysh'' Tribe in negotiation with any other clan on a political question. He used to represent the interest of his tribe in the capacit
2 CONC y of an Ambassador; also of being an Arbitrator between two contending chieftains, and pronouncing judgments in suits of litigants of the highest rank devolved upon him. When feud arose between '''Imaam 'Abd al-Muttalib bin Imaam 
2 CONC Hashim''' [the grandfather of the '''Prophet Muhammad (PBUH)'''] and '''Harb bin Umayya''' over the leadership of the tribe, both accepted '''Nufayl bin 'Abd al-`Uzza''' as their arbitrator, and he pronounced in favour of '''Imaam
2 CONC  'Abd al-Muttalib bin Imaam Hashim'''.
