1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattab
2 CONT
2 CONT    His mother was Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd ibn Mas'ud of Thaqif, whose mother was 'Atika bint Usayd, whose mother was Zaynab bint Abi 'Amr.  His children were 'Umar, whose mother was Zaynab bint Abi 'Amr.  His children were 'Umar,
2 CONC  whose mother was Umm Salama bint al-Mukhtar who was governor of Madina; 'Abdu'r-Rahman, Ibrahim, and Umm 'Abdu'r-Rahman, whose mother was Umm 'Abdullah bint 'Abdu'r-Rahman; and Riyah, whose mother was Habbaba bint 'Abdullah.  He 
2 CONC was the executor of his father's will, who was 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Nafi' said, '"Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah used to wear silk/wool, and Ibn 'Umar put his hand on him to lean on him and he did not object to it."
2 CONT
2 CONT    Muhammad ibn 'Umar said, "Abdullah died at the beginning of the Khalifate of Hisham ibn 'Abdul-Malik in Madina. He was reliable with few hadiths.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: The Men of Madina Vol. II, page 130
