1 CONT The name Seti means "of Set", which indicates that he was consecrated to the god Set. As with most Pharaohs, Seti had a number of names. Upon his ascension, he took the prenomen, which has the technical transliteration of mn-m3‘t-
1 CONC r‘. This is usually realised as Menmaatre, meaning "Established one of Maat and Ra". His better known nomen, or birth name is technically transliterated as sty mry-n-pt?, which is usually realised as Sety Meryenptah, meaning "Man 
1 CONC of Set, beloved of Ptah". The Greeks called him Sethosis. Manetho incorrectly considered him the founder of the 19th dynasty and estimated his reign to have lasted either 51 or 55 years.
