0 @N6000000002187600329@ NOTE Arshak I of Iberia
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Arshak I (Arsaces) (d. 81 BC) was king of Caucasian Iberia (93-81 BC) and founder of the Arsacid dynasty in Iberia, unrelated to the Arsacid Dynasty of Parthia and the later Arshakuni Dynasty of Armenia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Son of King Artavasdes I of Armenia, he was raised to the Iberian throne after King Farnadjom of Iberia had been deposed and killed in 93 BC.
1 CONT
1 CONT Under his rule, Iberia became a client state of Armenia and lost some of the western provinces to Colchis.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was succeeded as king of Iberia by his son Artag.
1 CONT
1 CONT
