0 @N6000000002188193523@ NOTE Abd-Allah ibn Abd-al-Muttalib
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Abd al-Mu??alib (Arabic: ??????? ?? ??? ????????)? (545-570) was the father of Muhammad, the prophet of Islam. He was the son of Shaiba ibn Hashim (`Abd al-Muttalib), and was married to Aminah bint Wahab. He died o
1 CONC n a caravan trip between Medina and Mecca.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was famed for his beauty. [citation needed] His name included the word Allah before Islam was founded. During the period before Islam, pagan Arabs called God as Allah in Arabic (and in Aramaic).
1 CONT
1 CONT His full lineage is:
1 CONT '''??????? ?? ??? ?????? ??? ???? ?? ??? ???? ?? ??? ?? ???? ?? ??? ?? ??? ?? ??? ?? ???? ??? ??? ?? ???? ?? ????? ?? ????? ?? ????? ?? ????? ?? ????? ?? ??? ?? ???? ?? ??? ?? ?????'''
1 CONT
1 CONT In Latin script, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdul Muttalib (Shaiba) ibn Hashim (Amr) ibn Abd Manaf (al-Mughira) ibn Qusai (Zaid) ibn Kilab ibn Murra ibn Ka`b ibn Lu'ay ibn Ghalib ibn Fahr (Quraish) ibn Malik ibn an-Nadr (Qais) ibn Kinana ibn 
1 CONC Khuzaimah ibn Mudrikah (Amir) ibn Ilyas ibn Mudar ibn Nizar ibn Ma`ad ibn Adnan. (ibn means "son of" in Arabic; alternate names of people with two names are given in parentheses.)
0 @N6000000002188182918@ NOTE Harb ibn Umayya
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Harb ibn Umayya was among the Sahaba's ancestors. Harb means "war".
1 CONT
1 CONT His father was Umayya ibn Abd Shams [1]
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the father of Harith ibn Harb and Abu Sufyan ibn Harb [2].
0 @N6000000002188182884@ NOTE Wa'il ibn Umayyah
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Wa'il ibn Umayya, also known as Abu al-As [citation needed] was the son of Umayya ibn Abd Shams.
1 CONT
1 CONT As his sons are mentioned:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * A'as ibn Wa'il, father of Amr ibn al-A'as[citation needed]
1 CONT     * Affan ibn Wa'il, father of Uthman[citation needed]
1 CONT     * Abu al-Hakim ibn Wa'il[citation needed]
1 CONT
1 CONT Another source also mentions:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Hakam ibn Wa'il, also known as "al-Hakam ibn Abi al-`As" [1] aka "Hakam Ibn Abi al-As Ibn Umayya" [2][citation needed]
1 CONT
1 CONT He also had a daughter:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Saffya binte abi al-A'as, who bore a daughter to Abu Safyan.
